{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"ALSA-2026:54530","published":"2026-08-13T00:00:00Z","modified":"2026-09-14T11:30:03.020912944Z","related":["CVE-2026-11822","CVE-2026-11824","CVE-2026-14257","CVE-2026-69152","CVE-2026-69192"],"summary":"Important: nodejs:22 security update","details":"Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language.   \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution via crafted FTS5 full-text search data (CVE-2026-11822)\n  * sqlite: SQLite: Arbitrary code execution and crash via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5 (CVE-2026-11824)\n  * brace-expansion: Brace-expansion: Denial of Service via memory exhaustion in expand() function (CVE-2026-14257)\n  * brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via unbounded intermediate arrays (CVE-2026-69152)\n  * ip-address: ip-address: Inconsistent IP address parsing leads to Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) and trust-boundary bypass (CVE-2026-69192)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"nodejs","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/nodejs"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:22.23.1-3.module_el8.10.0+4251+b427b8a5"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:54530.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-devel","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/almalinux/nodejs-devel"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1:22.23.1-3.module_el8.10.0+4251+b427b8a5"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/AlmaLinux/osv-database/blob/master/advisories/almalinux8/ALSA-2026:54530.json"}},{"package":{"name":"nodejs-docs","ecosystem":"AlmaLinux:8","purl":"pkg:r